<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

	<PropertyGroup>
		<TargetFramework>net8.0</TargetFramework>
		<ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
		<Nullable>enable</Nullable>
		<GeneratePackageOnBuild>True</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
		<Version>0.15.0</Version>
		<Authors>Codeer</Authors>
		<Company>Codeer</Company>
		<Description>Server-side services for Codeer.LowCode.Blazor apps. Includes AI document analysis (Azure Document Intelligence + Azure OpenAI), mail sending (SMTP / Microsoft Graph / SendGrid / Gmail), file storage (file system / Azure Blob / S3), external logins (Entra ID / Google / AWS Cognito / OIDC), TOTP two-factor authentication, and ASP.NET Core helpers (hot reload, ETag file responses).</Description>
		<PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/Codeer-Software/Codeer.LowCode.Blazor.Extras</PackageProjectUrl>
		<RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/Codeer-Software/Codeer.LowCode.Blazor.Extras</RepositoryUrl>
		<RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
		<PackageTags>Blazor;LowCode;Codeer;AI;Mail;Excel;PDF;OpenIdConnect;EntraID</PackageTags>
		<PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
		<PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>True</PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>
		<PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
		<PackageReleaseNotes>New: EditHistoryRecorder for EditHistoryField (Codeer.LowCode.Blazor.Extras 0.16.0).SubmitAsync(transactionData, () =&gt; base.SubmitAsync(transactionId, transactionData)) as in the app templates. For every root record of a submit whose module has an EditHistoryField it writes one row into the history module named by the field: for a delete the record as it was before (read before the base submit), for a create or update the record as saved (read back after the base submit, with the owned records loaded recursively without paging). A failure to record makes the submit fail (rollback), and so does a module whose history module or contract is missing. ExecuteSqlField saves are recorded too: Update and Delete timings as usual, a Create timing only when NewId returns the new Id, and a Standalone submit (SQL only, no rows) only when the record itself changed (the record is compared before and after). Requires Codeer.LowCode.Blazor.Extras 0.16.0. The recorder also performs the undeletes requested by the client (EditHistoryUndeleteData in ModuleSubmitData.ExtendedData) through ModuleDataIO.UndeleteAsync of Codeer.LowCode.Blazor 1.3.37 before the base submit, so revived rows are updated in the same transaction; a restored record is recorded as a Restore version. The snapshot is read with ModuleDataIO.the internal read of Codeer.LowCode.Blazor 1.3.37 (owned records declared by IOwnedRecordsFieldDesign, recursively). A submit that writes nothing (no add, update or delete; for example an approval submit of an unchanged request) is not recorded as a version. The change date is written like CreatedAt of the framework: in UTC when the DateTime field of the history module has SaveAsUtc, otherwise in server local time. The child record of an embedded module (ModuleField) is part of the snapshot through the owned-record declaration of ModuleFieldDesign in Codeer.LowCode.Blazor 1.3.37 (all its columns and its own owned records, also inside owned rows). Owned records that EditHistoryField leaves out (ExcludedOwnedRecords) or records per row (IndividuallyRecordedOwnedRecords) are not read into the parent's snapshot; per-row records are written to the row module's history for every row the submit added, updated or deleted (a delete is recorded with the row as it was), and a submit that changes only such rows (excluded or per-row) makes no version of the parent. EditHistoryRecorder now records the whole record regardless of the permissions of the user who saved it (ModuleDataIO.GetWithOwnedRecordsForInternalAsync of Codeer.LowCode.Blazor 1.3.37) and strips the snapshot to the permissions of the reader when the history module is read: wire EditHistoryRecorder.GetListAsync into CustomizedModuleDataIO.GetListAsync (now virtual) next to SubmitAsync; unreadable columns and the owned records of unreadable child modules are removed, and the snapshot is empty for a reader who cannot read the target module. EditHistoryRecorder is now an IModuleDataIOInterceptor of Codeer.LowCode.Blazor 1.3.37: register it once with ModuleDataIO.AddInterceptor(new EditHistoryRecorder(designData)) and it covers both the recording on save and the stripping of the snapshot to the reader's permissions on every read (no SubmitAsync / GetListAsync overrides, no AddSystemRecordAsync). Restore is done by the server from the history row: the client sends only the history row Id (EditHistoryUndeleteData.HistoryModuleName / HistoryRowId / RestoreWholeRecord), the server rebuilds the record from that version's snapshot (logical delete: undelete keeping the Ids; physical delete: recreated with new Ids, including the owned rows re-pointed to the new parent) and checks the reverse of delete (CanDelete, UserWrite and the row conditions) for every row; a version of another record is rejected. When a parent is deleted, the Delete versions of its individually recorded rows are written as well, regardless of how the delete was sent. Restore rules: a record is restored only from the latest version of the record (a Delete version followed by a Restore or a change is rejected); logical delete keeps the Ids and revives the rows deleted together with the parent with the rule of the delete itself (CanDelete of the child module only; physically deleted child rows are recreated); physical delete recreates the record with the original Id when the Id is entered manually (rejected when a record with that Id exists) and with a new Id otherwise, in which case the versions of the old Id are re-pointed to the new Id so the history stays continuous (the only case where history rows are updated; recreated child rows with their own history are treated the same); the child of an embedded module (ModuleField) is not recreated but referenced again (recreated only when it is gone). "Restore this version" revives only the rows of the version that are deleted now and visible to the user and fails as a whole when one cannot be revived. Submits that add or update rows of a history module are rejected (versions are written by the system only; deletes are allowed). Undelete requires UserRead like delete. Per-row Delete versions written on a parent delete are read with the row module's own policy. Requires Codeer.LowCode.Blazor 1.3.37 with ModuleDataIOInternalAccess.GetListAsync / UpdateAsync / UndeleteTogetherAsync.</PackageReleaseNotes>
		<PackageId>Codeer.LowCode.Blazor.Extras.Server</PackageId>
		<!-- NU5104: Azure.AI.OpenAI has no stable release built for the OpenAI 2.9+ line yet, so the prerelease dependency is intentional -->
		<NoWarn>$(NoWarn);NU5104</NoWarn>
	</PropertyGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<FrameworkReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.App" />
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<!-- internal のテストのみに許可 (製品アセンブリへの IVT は不可) -->
		<AssemblyAttribute Include="System.Runtime.CompilerServices.InternalsVisibleTo">
			<_Parameter1>Codeer.LowCode.Blazor.Extras.Test</_Parameter1>
		</AssemblyAttribute>
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<ProjectReference Include="..\Codeer.LowCode.Blazor.Extras\Codeer.LowCode.Blazor.Extras.csproj" />
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<!-- メールプレビュー HTML (MailPreviewHtml が埋め込みから読む) -->
		<EmbeddedResource Include="Mail\MailPreview.html" LogicalName="Codeer.LowCode.Blazor.Extras.Server.Mail.MailPreview.html" />
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<PackageReference Include="Azure.AI.FormRecognizer" Version="4.1.0" />
		<PackageReference Include="Azure.AI.OpenAI" Version="2.9.0-beta.1" />
		<PackageReference Include="AWSSDK.S3" Version="4.0.102.4" />
		<PackageReference Include="Azure.Identity" Version="1.13.2" />
		<PackageReference Include="Azure.Storage.Blobs" Version="12.23.0" />
		<PackageReference Include="Excel.Report.PDF" Version="0.36.0" />
		<PackageReference Include="MailKit" Version="4.17.0" />
		<PackageReference Include="Markdig" Version="0.37.0" />
		<PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.AI" Version="10.7.0" />
		<PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.AI.OpenAI" Version="10.7.0" />
		<PackageReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authentication.OpenIdConnect" Version="8.0.8" />
		<PackageReference Include="System.Text.Encoding.CodePages" Version="8.0.0" />
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<None Include="..\..\README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
		<None Include="..\..\LICENSE" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<EmbeddedResource Update="Properties\Resources.resx">
			<Generator>ResXFileCodeGenerator</Generator>
			<LastGenOutput>Resources.Designer.cs</LastGenOutput>
		</EmbeddedResource>
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<Compile Update="Properties\Resources.Designer.cs">
			<DesignTime>True</DesignTime>
			<AutoGen>True</AutoGen>
			<DependentUpon>Resources.resx</DependentUpon>
		</Compile>
	</ItemGroup>

</Project>
